From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Greg Daniel <egdaniel@google.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:30:36 -0500
Subject: [M156] Reject fractional Slug replay for direct masks when atlas
 bilerp is unsupported

Original change's description:
> Reject fractional Slug replay for direct masks when atlas bilerp is unsupported
>
> When fSupportBilerpFromGlyphAtlas is false (e.g. Chrome's configuration),
> direct-mask glyphs are packed in the shared TextAtlasManager with 0
> padding. Replaying a Slug with a fractional translation or incompatible
> matrix causes sampling outside the glyph's atlas boundaries under MSAA,
> leaking neighboring glyph texels across origins.
>
> 1. Promote Slug matrix validation to release mode via SlugImpl::canDraw
>    in both Ganesh and Graphite Device::drawSlug, dropping draws when
>    the matrix difference includes non-integer translation or transform
>    without atlas bilerp support.
> 2. In VertexFiller::boundsAndDeviceMatrix, return empty bounds for direct
>    masks when supportBilerpAtlas is false and the transform is not an
>    integer translation, dropping the draw and preventing any fractional
>    maskToDevice from reaching the GPU.
> 3. Add unit tests for VertexFiller::boundsAndDeviceMatrix and end-to-end
>    fractional Slug replay validation in Ganesh and Graphite.
>
> Bug: 576950618
